@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+# Separate checkout entries
+
+GUI-only patch for OpenCode **v2.2.6** (`dc2ffcf8bf26f9e669b6aa22b95f50e12be15e06`) and **v2.2.7** (`fedc6f208aa2bd54c1019227214568083f6380ad`).
+
+Use **Add project** for each permanent clone or checkout. Directories sharing a repository ID stay separate in Home, Settings > Projects, the New Session picker, and the organized sidebar. Selecting Local in a new session targets the selected checkout, not the repository's canonical clone.
+
+Checkout entries survive reloads and can be closed independently. Secondary checkouts default to their folder name and can be renamed independently. Their labels are client-local. Icon colors and uploaded images are client-local for secondary checkouts and for the primary checkout when multiple entries share its repository. Local icon choices survive reloads and closing sibling entries. Single-entry primary projects retain server-backed appearance settings. The primary project's name, commands, repository identity, and session IDs remain server-backed. Other repository-level settings remain shared.
+
+This patch does not create, copy, allocate, recycle, delete, or switch any checkout. Prepare the directories and switch their branches yourself. Two entries pointing to the same directory do not provide isolation.
+
+## Build and try without replacing the installed app
+
+Use Bun 1.4.4, pinned by the repository. From the repository root:
+
+```sh
+bun install --frozen-lockfile
+cd packages/app
+VITE_OPENCODE_SERVER_MODE=none bun run build
+bun run serve -- --host 127.0.0.1 --port 4444
+```
+
+Open <http://127.0.0.1:4444> and connect to the existing OpenCode 2.2.6 server using its address and sign-in/pairing flow. This is a separate browser client: it has its own project preferences, while sessions stay on the existing server. Do not start a replacement backend. The `none` build mode prevents the static preview from being mistaken for an API server.
+
+The same app source is used by the Electron renderer. Native desktop build and packaging instructions are in `packages/desktop/README.md`; a native installer is not included here. No installed application or running service is modified by this patch or the browser build.
+
+## Validation
+
+```sh
+# Repository lint and package typechecks (from repository root)
+bun run check
+
+# App unit tests (from packages/app)
+bun run test:unit
+
+# Production-build browser regression suite (from packages/app)
+bun x playwright install chromium
+PLAYWRIGHT_BUILD=1 bun x playwright test e2e/regression/home.spec.ts --project chromium
+```
+
+The clone regression adds a secondary directory through the folder picker, reloads, selects each checkout independently, submits a session and checks its exact directory, renames the secondary checkout, customizes colors and an uploaded icon independently, reloads again, and closes only that entry. Registry tests cover persisted entries with a shared project ID, independent labels, last selection, and removal. Existing tests cover older preference migration and delayed desktop storage.
+
+The separate `typecheck:e2e` command currently reports unrelated existing fixture/type errors and missing Vite asset declarations. The canonical repository check and app typecheck are the supported checks for production source.
